{"step_index":231,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:53:01Z","content":"### Summary of Results\n\nThe conjecture in [`Challenge_1facfd37.lean`](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_1facfd37/Challenge_1facfd37.lean) has been settled by **proof** (`prove_1facfd37 : Candidate`).\n\n#### Mathematical Idea\nFor any finite simple graph $G = (V, E)$:\n1. Let $I \\subseteq V$ be any independent set and let $s \\subseteq E$ be any edge cover of $G$.\n2. Since $s$ covers all vertices of $G$, for each vertex $v \\in I$ there exists an edge $e \\in s$ such that $v \\in e$.\n3. We define an assignment $f : I \\to s$ choosing an edge $f(v) \\in s$ incident to $v$.\n4. If $f(u) = f(v) = e$ for distinct vertices $u, v \\in I$, then both endpoints of edge $e$ lie in $I$, implying that $u$ and $v$ are adjacent in $G$. This contradicts the independence of $I$. Hence $f$ is injective.\n5. Injective assignment yields $|I| \\le |s|$.\n6. Bounding over all independent sets and valid edge covers establishes that $\\text{indepNum}(G) \\le \\text{edgeCoverNumber}(G)$.\n\n#### Verification\nChecked with `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_1facfd37.lean`:\n\n```\nLINT: ok\n/tmp/tmp.z05v25CXN9.lean:86:8: warning: declaration uses `sorry`\n'prove_1facfd37' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'refute_1facfd37' depends on axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\nCHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\n       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\n```\n\nThe report has been written to [`REPORT.md`](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_1facfd37/REPORT.md)."}
